+# Implementation Plan: Rental Module
+
+**Spec**: [spec.md](spec.md)
+
+## Technical Context
+- TypeScript (ES2022, NodeNext, strict), Node.js stdlib only, in-memory state.
+- Tests: `node:test` + `node:assert`; TypeScript compiled with `tsc` (devDependencies `typescript`, `@types/node`), tests run from `dist/`.
+- Booking ids from `node:crypto` `randomUUID` (stdlib; non-deterministic but only required to be unique).
+
+## Constitution Check
+- I No runtime deps: pass (devDependencies only).
+- II Strict ESM TS: pass; `.js` import extensions.
+- III Tests with behavior: `test/rental.test.ts`, deterministic (no clock used).
+- IV Explicit rules: day/period rule in one named function `parsePeriod`; UTC parsing explicit; no guessed rules (see spec Assumptions).
+- V Simplicity: one module `src/rental.ts`, re-exported by `src/index.ts`.
+Post-design: still passes.
+
+## Design
+- `src/rental.ts`: types `Equipment`, `RentalRequest`, `Quote`, `Booking`; `createRentalService()`.
+- Period validation: strict regex `YYYY-MM-DDT00:00:00(.000)?Z`, round-trip through `Date` to reject impossible dates; end > start; days = diff / 86400000.
+- Total = dailyPrice × days (integers). Overlap: `start < other.end && other.start < end`.
+- Returned start/end are the request strings. Cancellation not implemented.
+- Build: `tsconfig` includes `src` only; add `tsconfig.test.json`? Simpler: change `include` to `["src","test"]` and `npm test` = `tsc && node --test dist`.
+
+## Artifacts
+No separate research/contracts: the contract is the request in the spec; data model is the Key Entities in spec.
+Quickstart: `npm install && npm test`.
