+# Feature Specification: Rental Module
+
+**Feature Directory**: `specs/001-rental-module`
+**Input**: Booking desk needs a rental module for boards and sails (in-memory, basics only).
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing *(mandatory)*
+
+### User Story 1 - Register equipment (Priority: P1)
+The desk registers a rentable item with an id, a kind (board or sail) and a daily price.
+
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+1. **Given** an empty service, **When** a board `b1` at 2500 cents/day is added, **Then** it can be quoted and booked.
+
+### User Story 2 - Quote a rental (Priority: P1)
+The desk asks what renting an item for a period costs.
+
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+1. **Given** `b1` at 2500, **When** quoting 2026-06-01T00:00:00Z to 2026-06-04T00:00:00Z, **Then** total is 7500.
+2. **Given** an unknown item or a period that is not whole UTC days, **When** quoting, **Then** an error is thrown.
+
+### User Story 3 - Book a rental (Priority: P1)
+The desk books an item for a period and gets a booking with an id and total.
+
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+1. **Given** a free item, **When** booked, **Then** `{ id, itemId, start, end, total }` is returned.
+2. **Given** an existing booking, **When** booking an overlapping period for the same item, **Then** an error is thrown.
+3. **Given** an existing booking, **When** booking the period starting at its end, or another item, **Then** it succeeds.
+
+### Edge Cases
+- End not after start, or zero-length period: rejected.
+- Times not at midnight UTC, not valid ISO-8601, or without UTC designation: rejected.
+- Invalid equipment (non-integer or negative price, unknown kind, empty or duplicate id): rejected.
+- A failed booking leaves no trace.
+
+## Requirements *(mandatory)*
+
+### Functional Requirements
+- **FR-001**: `createRentalService()` is exported from `src/index.ts` and returns an in-memory service.
+- **FR-002**: `addEquipment({ id, kind, dailyPrice })` registers an item; kind is `'board'` or `'sail'`.
+- **FR-003**: `quote({ itemId, start, end })` returns `{ itemId, start, end, total }`, total = daily price × number of days.
+- **FR-004**: `book(request)` returns `{ id, itemId, start, end, total }` with a unique booking id.
+- **FR-005**: `quote` and `book` throw for an unknown item or a disallowed period; `book` also throws when the item is booked for any overlapping time.
+- **FR-006**: Money is an integer number of euro cents.
+- **FR-007**: Times are ISO-8601 UTC strings.
+- **FR-008**: Periods are whole days: start and end at midnight UTC, end after start, end being the start of the day after the last day.
+- **FR-009**: The same item is never booked for overlapping periods (back-to-back is not overlapping).
+- **FR-010**: Cancellation is NOT implemented. The policy (cancelled <24h before start: no refund; otherwise full refund) is recorded for later.
+
+### Key Entities
+- **Equipment**: id, kind, dailyPrice.
+- **Booking**: id, itemId, start, end, total.
+
+## Success Criteria *(mandatory)*
+
+### Measurable Outcomes
+- **SC-001**: Quotes equal daily price × days for every valid period tested.
+- **SC-002**: No two bookings of one item overlap, in all tested conflict cases.
+- **SC-003**: Every invalid input listed in the edge cases is rejected.
+
+## Assumptions
+- Season (April–October) is not enforced; the request does not ask for it.
+- No student/visitor price difference in this request.
+- Booking ids are opaque unique strings.
+- The earliest/latest allowed dates are unconstrained, and past dates are allowed (no clock involved).
